# check_ARGO_sync.py — Scope Filtering Flags

**Audience:** Whoever maintains the check and the Icinga config (Lee, Steven)
**Applies to:** `check_ARGO_sync.py` with `--cluster` / `--project` / `--dest-namespace` / `--annotation`

---

## 1. What each flag matches

The flags do **exact string match** (no substring, no wildcard) against these JSON fields:

| Flag | JSON field | Value from our actual API sample |
|---|---|---|
| `--cluster` | `spec.destination.server` **or** `spec.destination.name` | `https://kubernetes.default.svc` (in-cluster) |
| `--project` | `spec.project` | `master-app`, `snd-linuxadmin` |
| `--dest-namespace` | `spec.destination.namespace` | `openshift-gitops`, `snd-linuxadmin-hl-nginx-canary` |
| `--annotation` | `metadata.annotations` (KEY=VALUE) | (none in the sample) |

This is why the earlier attempts returned zero matches:

```
--project snd        ->  no app has project exactly "snd"      (they are "snd-linuxadmin", ...)
--cluster os4snd     ->  no app has cluster exactly "os4snd"   (it is "https://kubernetes.default.svc")
```

`snd` is a *prefix* of the real values, and the filter does not do prefix matching.

Working commands against the sample data:

```bash
python3 check_ARGO_sync.py -d '<context>' --project snd-linuxadmin
python3 check_ARGO_sync.py -d '<context>' --project master-app
python3 check_ARGO_sync.py -d '<context>' --cluster https://kubernetes.default.svc
python3 check_ARGO_sync.py -d '<context>' --dest-namespace openshift-gitops
```

> **Note on `--cluster`:** apps deployed to the hub itself always use the
> in-cluster URL `https://kubernetes.default.svc`. Apps targeting spoke
> clusters carry that cluster's full API URL (e.g.
> `https://api.os4snd.hobbylobby.corp:6443`) or the name the cluster was
> registered under in ArgoCD (`spec.destination.name`). The flag accepts
> either form.

