## 4. Icinga configuration — values as variables, not hardcoded

The flag values belong in **host custom variables**. The script and the CheckCommand never contain a project or cluster name.

**Step 1 — CheckCommand (define once, never edit again):**

```
object CheckCommand "check_argo_sync" {
  command = [ PluginDir + "/check_ARGO_sync.py" ]

  arguments = {
    "-d"               = { value = "$argo_context$" }
    "--cluster"        = { value = "$argo_cluster$"    repeat_key = true }
    "--project"        = { value = "$argo_project$"    repeat_key = true }
    "--dest-namespace" = { value = "$argo_dest_ns$"    repeat_key = true }
    "--annotation"     = { value = "$argo_annotation$" repeat_key = true }
  }
}
```

`repeat_key = true` makes an **array** custom var expand into repeated flags —
`vars.argo_project = [ "a", "b" ]` becomes `--project a --project b`. That is
the Icinga-side equivalent of the script's `action="append"`.

**Step 2 — put the scope definitions in host vars (the ONLY place values live):**

```
object Host "argocd-hub" {
  check_command = "hostalive"

  vars.argo_context = "default/api-os4hub-hobbylobby-corp:6443/system:serviceaccount:default:svcicinga"

  // one entry per Icinga service you want; edit THIS block to add/remove scopes
  vars.argo_scopes["snd-linuxadmin"] = {
    argo_project = [ "snd-linuxadmin" ]
  }
  vars.argo_scopes["master-app"] = {
    argo_project = [ "master-app" ]
  }
  vars.argo_scopes["in-cluster"] = {
    argo_cluster = [ "https://kubernetes.default.svc" ]
  }
}
```

**Step 3 — generate the services with `apply for` (define once, never edit again):**

```
apply Service "argo-sync-" for (scope => config in host.vars.argo_scopes) {
  check_command = "check_argo_sync"
  vars.argo_context = host.vars.argo_context
  vars += config

  assign where host.vars.argo_scopes
}
```

This produces services `argo-sync-snd-linuxadmin`, `argo-sync-master-app`,
`argo-sync-in-cluster` — each with its own state, notifications, and perfdata
stream.

**Maintenance workflow when projects/clusters change:**

1. Run the discovery commands in §3 to see what exists now
2. Add/remove/rename entries in the `vars.argo_scopes` block — one place, a few lines
3. `icinga2 daemon -C && systemctl reload icinga2`

Nothing else changes. The script, the CheckCommand, and the `apply for` rule are all value-free.

