## 5. How flags combine

| Combination | Semantics |
|---|---|
| Same flag repeated (`--project a --project b`) | OR — matches either |
| Different flags together (`--project a --cluster x`) | AND — must match both |
| Flag not given | No filter on that field |
| `--annotation k1=v1 --annotation k2=v2` | AND — both annotations required |

---

## 6. Troubleshooting zero matches

The UNKNOWN message distinguishes the two failure modes:

| Message | Meaning | Action |
|---|---|---|
| `Failed to retrieve ArgoCD applications` | oc returned nothing — ArgoCD/auth problem | Check context, kubeconfig, service account |
| `No applications matched filter (...) - N exist unfiltered` | ArgoCD is fine; the filter value is wrong | Re-run §3 discovery, copy the exact value |

Remember: exact match. `snd` ≠ `snd-linuxadmin`. When in doubt, copy-paste from the discovery output rather than typing.

---

## 7. Known limitations

1. **Exact match only.** Selecting "everything snd-*" requires listing each snd project explicitly (or adding a prefix/regex mode to the script — not currently implemented; ask if wanted).
2. **ApplicationSets are filtered implicitly** via their parent Application, since the `status.resources[]` stubs carry no spec of their own. An AppSet appears in the result iff its parent Application passed the filter.
3. **Small scopes are more sensitive.** The >20% CRITICAL threshold applies to the filtered population — with 4 apps in scope, one OutOfSync app is 25% and goes straight to CRITICAL.
